# tests/IR_XFAIL — files that fail under --use-ir-codegen during M3 milestone.
#
# Format: one path per line, optional `# reason` after the path.
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. Blank lines ignored.
#
# When a file is removed from this list, the corresponding M3 PR has closed
# its parity gap. CI's test-ir job uses this to compute pass/fail:
#   - file in XFAIL + fails  → counted as xfail (OK)
#   - file in XFAIL + passes → "unexpected OK" (remove from XFAIL)
#   - file not in XFAIL + fails → unexpected failure (CI fails once gate is blocking)
#
# Validate this file with: bash scripts/check_ir_xfail.sh
#
# Closed gates (M3 milestone, in order):
#   PR 2 — CPR ctor lowering (boxed)              ✓ #47
#   PR 3 — TUnary `!` + `-`, binary `/`           ✓ #48
#   PR 4 — short-circuit `&&` / `||`              ✓ #49
#   PR 5 — top-level let bindings (module-init)   ✓ #50
#   PR 6 — top-level fn eta wrappers              ✓ #51
#   PR 7 — tuple expressions + TuplePattern       ✓ this PR
#   PR 8 — nested constructor patterns            ✓ this PR
#   PR 9 — String equality `==` / `!=`            ✓ this PR
#
# Bucket breakdown after PR 9 closes (re-probed):
#   74 entries — Bool and Unit cannot be passed as i64
#                (String eq cleared; Bool/Unit call-arg ABI now dominates)
#   10 entries — do-block + IO + main body (milestone-level blocker)
#    2 entries — pre-existing direct-codegen xfails (unresolved names in source)

